json PermitReceipe {
  doc """
  One synthesis recipe the player is allowed to craft.  Emitted in UserInfo
  under 51yQrDBR (PermitRecipeResponse).

  This list IS the synthesis menu.  MyTownItemListScene::setRecipeList
  (0x18E9434) and its sphere twin walk PermitRecipeInfoList — never
  RecipeMstList — and resolve each permitted id against the recipe master, so a
  missing 51yQrDBR renders an empty Synthesis facility.  The server derives the
  set from the player's town facility levels via TownFacilityLvMst.release_recipe.

  Setters are PermitRecipeInfo::set* (libgame.so 0x126D388..0x126D50C).
  """

  field recipe_id type="i32::str" {
    key "4HqhTf3a"
    doc """
    The JOIN KEY.  readParam feeds setRecipeID(string) @0x13E9C60;
    PermitRecipeInfoList::getObjectWithRecipeID @0x126D840 matches it against
    RecipeMst::getRecipeID.  Also read by MyTownItemListScene::setRecipeList
    @0x18E957C / downloadFiles @0x18E8C5C, MyTownSphereListScene::setFilterRecipeList
    @0x1906530, ItemMixScene::getRecipeList @0x1704F9C, and the NEW-badge flags
    BadgeInfo::newFlagItemRecipe @0x11F1FA8 / newFlagSphereRecipe @0x11F2384 /
    newFlagLSSphereRecipe @0x11F262C / newFlagRaidItem @0x11F31BC.
    """
  }

  field craft_count type="i32::str" {
    key "H6k1LIxC"
    doc """
    Crafts ALREADY PERFORMED — a tally, not a cap.  Confirmed by arithmetic,
    not by the setter name:

      * GameUtils::isMixSphereCnt @0x1177604 returns RecipeMst.vtbl[0x28]() >
        getCnt() — the MST holds the cap, this holds the count.
      * GameUtils::updatePermitRecipe @0x1177C8C does setCnt(getCnt() + 1)
        after each craft, so the server reports the persisted total.
      * MyTownItemListScene::setRecipeList @0x18E96C0 HIDES the recipe once
        cap <= getCnt().

    Two edge cases in isMixSphereCnt: a cap of -1 means unlimited @0x117761C,
    and NO PermitRecipeInfo row at all returns 0 = uncraftable @0x1177614 —
    which is why a missing 51yQrDBR renders an empty Synthesis facility.
    """
  }

  field available_seconds type="i32::str" {
    key "VDKB0Y5h"
    doc """
    SECONDS REMAINING in this recipe's availability window, not a craft cap.
    setLimit @0x126D4A4 stores the value and stamps CommonUtils::getNowUnitxTime();
    getRemainingTime @0x126D4CC returns -1 unchanged when negative @0x126D4FC,
    otherwise max(0, limit - elapsed) @0x126D4F4.

    -1 means "permanent" and is what the timeless recipes need
    (ReceipeMst.availability_end is 9999-12-31 for those).  SENDING 0 HIDES
    EVERY RECIPE: MyTownItemListScene::setRecipeList discriminates the two
    explicitly — == -1 keeps the row @0x18E96CC, then < 1 skips it @0x18E96E0.
    Same epoch-zero trap as handbook 6.12.

    RecipeListBaseScene::setItemLimitTime @0x18FD1A8 draws the countdown label
    only when >= 1.  The raw accessor getLimit @0x126D49C has ZERO call sites —
    the value reaches the UI only through getRemainingTime.
    """
  }

}